,"οἶδα"],["I do not know","ouk oida","OOK OY-dah","οὐκ οἶδα"],["he is good","agathos esti","ah-gah-THOS ES-tee","ἀγαθός ἐστι"],["he is not good","ouk agathos esti","OOK ah-gah-THOS ES-tee","οὐκ ἀγαθός ἐστι"],["do not say","me lege","MAY LEH-geh","μὴ λέγε"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["The second-person singular command is usually the bare stem: lege (say!), grapse (write!). Plural adds -ete: legete."],"rows":[["say!","lege","λέγε"],["write!","grapse","γράψον"],["come!","deuro","δεῦρο"]],"ex":[["come here","deuro","DEH-oo-ro","δεῦρο"],["say","lege","LEH-geh","λέγε"],["listen","akoue","ah-KOO-eh","ἄκουε"],["wait","mene","MEH-neh","μένε"]]},{"id":"questions","title":"Questions","text":["Add \"ara\" at the start for a yes or no question, or use a question word."],"rows":[["Is it...?","ara","ἆρα"]],"ex":[["is he a teacher?","ara didaskalos esti","AH-rah dee-DAS-kah-los ES-tee","ἆρα διδάσκαλός ἐστι;"],["what is this?","ti esti touto","tee ES-tee TOO-toh","τί ἐστι τοῦτο;"],["who are you?","tis ei","TIS AY","τίς εἶ;"]]}],"name":"Ancient Greek","id":"grc","flag":"gr","script":"Greek","note":""}